## 📂 Backend Directory Layout

```text
backend/
├── app/
│   ├── routes/               # Blueprint Controllers
│   │   ├── __init__.py
│   │   ├── admin.py          # Admin user management & moderation
│   │   ├── auth_profile.py   # Auth (Register, Login) & User Profile CRUD
│   │   ├── categories.py     # Category CRUD operations
│   │   ├── comment_reactions.py # Reactions (Likes/Dislikes) on comments
│   │   ├── comments.py       # Threaded comments & reviews
│   │   ├── content.py        # Core post creation & media handling
│   │   ├── interactions.py   # Likes, reviews & post interactions
│   │   ├── notifications.py  # User notification dispatches
│   │   ├── reports.py        # Content reporting & flag moderation
│   │   └── subscriptions.py  # Category subscription management
│   ├── static/               # Static assets & uploads
│   ├── __init__.py           # Flask app factory setup
│   ├── email_service.py      # SMTP Email sending service
│   ├── extensions.py         # SQLAlchemy, JWT, Bcrypt initializations
│   ├── models.py             # Database Models (User, Profile, Category, Post, Comment, etc.)
│   ├── schema.py             # Marshmallow schemas for serialization
│   ├── seed.py               # Database seeder script
│   └── utils.py              # Helper functions & RBAC decorators
├── migrations/               # Flask-Migrate database history
├── venv/                     # Python Virtual Environment
├── .env                      # Environment secrets
├── .env.example              # Sample environment template
├── .gitignore                # Git ignore rules
├── config.py                 # Environment configurations (Dev, Testing, Prod)
├── Pipfile                   # Pipenv dependency specification
├── Pipfile.lock              # Pipenv lockfile
├── README.md                 # Project documentation
├── requirements.txt          # Python dependencies manifesto
├── run.py                    # Application entry point
└── test_routes.py            # API route integration tests

## How to Run the Backend

1. Clone the repository and navigate to the backend directory.
2. Navigate to the backend directory:
    ```bash
    cd backend
    ```
3 Create a virtual environment and activate it:
    ```bash
    python -m venv venv
    source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows use `venv\Scripts\activate
    ```
4. Install the required dependencies:
    ```bash
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    If by chance that command does not work, you can try:
    python3/ python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
    ```
5. Set up the environment variables in the `.env` file.
    ```bash
    FLASK_APP=run.py
    FLASK_ENV=development
    SECRET_KEY=your-super-secret-key
    JWT_SECRET_KEY=your-jwt-secret-key
    DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:password@localhost:5432/moringa_daily_dev
    ```
6. Run the seeder script to populate the database with initial data:
    ```bash
    python3/ python seed.py
    ```
7. Run the database migrations:
    ```bash
    flask db upgrade
    ```
8. Start the Flask development server:
    ```bash
    python3/ python run.py
    ``` 
9. Access the API documentation at `http://localhost:5000/apidocs`.

# Testing with Curl
I tested with curl commands to ensure that the endpoints are working as expected. This is because the Swagger UI was not loading properly. Here are some example curl commands:
    1A. Authentication(Register new user):
    ```bash
    curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/auth/register" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -d '{
       "username": "Derrick Ogumba",
       "email": "derrick.ogumba@moringaschool.com",
       "password": "Password12345!",
       "role": "user"
     }'
     ```

    1B. Login and obtain JWT token:
    ```bash
    curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/auth/login" \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -d '{
            "email": "derrick.ogumba@moringaschool.com",
            "password": "Password12345!"
        }'
    ```
    1C. Get profile:
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/auth/me" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"
    ```
    2A. Create Categories:
    Create Category (Admin / Tech Writer)
    ```bash
    curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/categories" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
     -d '{
       "name": "DevOps",
       "description": "CI/CD pipelines, Docker, Kubernetes and Cloud Engineering"
     }'
     ```
     2B. Get Categories
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/categories" \
     -H "Accept: application/json"
    ```

    3. Subscriptions (routes/subscriptions.py):
    3A. Subscribe to Category
    ```bash
        curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/subscriptions" \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
        -d '{
        "category_id": 1
        }'
    ``` 
    3B. Unsubscribe from Category:
    ```bash
        curl -X DELETE "http://localhost:5001/api/subscriptions/1" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"
    ```
    3C. Unsubscribe from Category (alternative):
    ``` bash
    curl -X DELETE "http://localhost:5001/api/subscriptions/1" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN"
    ``` 
    4 . Create a new post (Tech Writer/user role required):
    4A. Create a new post
    ```bash
       curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/posts" \
     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
     -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
     -d '{
       "title": "Getting Started with Kubernetes",
       "category_id": 1,
       "type": "blog",
       "summary": "An introduction to container orchestration for Moringa alumni.",
       "body": "Markdown or text content here...",
       "media_url": "[https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/sample.mp4](https://res.cloudinary.com/demo/video/upload/sample.mp4)"
     }' 
    ```
    4B. Get all posts:
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/posts" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
    ```
    4C. Get a specific post by ID (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/posts/<POST_ID>" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
    ```


    5. Get all posts:
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/posts" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
    ```
    6. Get a specific post by ID (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/posts/<POST_ID>" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
    ``` 
    7. Update a post (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X PUT "http://localhost:5001/api/posts/<POST_ID>" \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>" \
        -d '{   
            "title": "Updated Post Title",
            "content": "This is the updated content of my post."
        }'
    ```
    8. Delete a post (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X DELETE "http://localhost:5001/api/posts/<POST_ID>" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
    ```
    9. Create a comment on a post (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X POST "http://localhost:5001/api/comments" \
        -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"
        -d '{
            "post_id": <POST_ID>,
            "content": "This is a comment on the post."
        }'
    ```
    10. Get comments for a specific post (replace `<POST_ID>` with the actual post ID):
    ```bash
    curl -X GET "http://localhost:5001/api/comments?post_id=<POST_ID>" \
        -H "Authorization: Bearer <JWT_TOKEN>"

    
